---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import {withBase} from '../lib/paths';
---

<DocsLayout
	title="FAQ"
	eyebrow="[ FAQ ]"
	description="Short answers to the questions humans and agents ask most."
>
	<h2>Is Kuyfi an auditor / certification?</h2>
	<p>
		No. Automated black-box / pre-audit tooling. Formal audits (Ottersec, Veridise, CoinFabrik,
		…) still matter.
	</p>

	<h2>Do I need Rust source?</h2>
	<p>No. Kuyfi works from deployed WASM and <code>contractspecv0</code>.</p>

	<h2>Does it work on Mainnet?</h2>
	<p>No. RPC is hardcoded to Stellar Testnet in v0.1.0. Mainnet is explicitly out of roadmap scope.</p>

	<h2>Will Chaos Monkey drain my wallet?</h2>
	<p>
		It uses ephemeral Friendbot-funded <strong>Testnet</strong> accounts. Fees are tiny Testnet
		XLM. Still only hit contracts you are allowed to test.
	</p>

	<h2>Why so many PRECONDITION / SECURE results?</h2>
	<p>
		Type-correct inputs are often not semantically valid (unauthorized signer, missing setup).
		Those outcomes are filtered from the findings list on purpose. See
		<a href={withBase('/findings')}>Findings</a> and
		<a href={withBase('/troubleshooting')}>Troubleshooting</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>What does POTENTIAL_VULN mean?</h2>
	<p>
		A security <em>signal</em> that needs contextual review — for example an access-control
		vector that was not rejected. It is <strong>not</strong> a confirmed exploit or CVE.
	</p>

	<h2>Can I expose Chaos Monkey on the paid API?</h2>
	<p>By design, no. Only the read-only scanner is HTTP-exposed.</p>

	<h2>JSON vs PDF — which is source of truth?</h2>
	<p>
		Neither “wins”: both are renders of the same <code>SecurityReport</code>. Prefer JSON for CI;
		see <a href={withBase('/report-schema')}>schema</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>My contract has no contractspec — can I scan?</h2>
	<p>
		OSINT depends on <code>contractspecv0</code>. Exotic/non-SDK builds may hit
		<code>XDR_ALIGN_FAILURE</code>. Rebuild with the Soroban SDK so the spec section is present.
	</p>

	<h2>How do agents / LLMs read the docs?</h2>
	<p>
		Use <strong>Markdown for Agents</strong> (plain Markdown) — not MDX.
		Start at <a href={withBase('/agent-setup')}>Agent setup</a>:
		<a href={withBase('/llms.txt')}>llms.txt</a> →
		<a href={withBase('/llms-full.txt')}>llms-full.txt</a> →
		<code>/docs/md/&lt;slug&gt;.md</code> or Page options → Copy as Markdown.
		Search: <kbd>⌘K</kbd>.
	</p>

	<h2>Is MCP ready?</h2>
	<p>
		Yes. A hosted MCP server is available (simulation only, sign in with GitHub) with five tools:
		<code>list_functions</code>, <code>scan_contract</code>, <code>fuzz_contract</code>,
		<code>get_report</code>, <code>report_card</code> —
		<a href={`${withBase('/mcp')}#connect`}>Conectar el MCP al server de Kuyfi</a>. The CLI and
		TUI remain the local alternative.
	</p>

	<h2>Where is the website / repo?</h2>
	<p>
		<a href="https://kuyfi.vercel.app">kuyfi.vercel.app</a> · Docs under <code>/docs</code> ·
		GitHub <a href="https://github.com/alex0tico/kuyfi">alex0tico/kuyfi</a> · npm
		<code>@kuyfi/kuyfi</code>.
	</p>
</DocsLayout>
